OL,3,GNEWSAThefts from woman with Alzheimer's
OL,4,Adevastate family                       
OL,6,FThe family of a woman who had early    
OL,7,Fonset Alzheimer's when her partner     
OL,8,Fstole thousands of pounds from her have
OL,9,Fsaid his crimes have "devastated" them.
OL,11,FDavid Brinded, 62, of Eaton, Norwich,  
OL,12,Fwas sentenced to 32 months in prison   
OL,13,Ffor fraud by abuse of position at      
OL,14,FNorwich Crown Court on Wednesday, after
OL,15,Fhe was found to have taken #21,500 from
OL,16,FRosalind Jeczalik to fund his          
OL,17,Flifestyle.                             
OL,19,FBrinded was sole power of attorney for 
OL,20,FJeczalik, who died in 2024 aged 70,    
OL,21,Feight years after she was diagnosed    
OL,22,Fwith the condition.                    
OL,23,APub: 27-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2 
